#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:121
#, python-brace-format
msgid "In an HCERT, claim key 5 holds the VHL payload as a CBOR map with text keys, conforming to the <a0>Verifiable Health Link Payload</a0> logical model. A CBOR map is used rather than a {code0} URI string because the URI form base64url-encodes JSON text inside the CBOR, which makes the QR code roughly a third larger."
msgstr ""

#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:143
msgid "In order for Verifiers to be able to detect the type of data encoded and to select the proper decoding and processing scheme, the base45 encoded data (as per this specification) SHALL be prefixed by the Context Identifier string \"HC1:\". Future versions of this specification that impact backwards-compatibility SHALL define a new Context Identifier, whereas the character following \"HC\" SHALL be taken from the character set [1-9A-Z]. The order of increments is defined to be in that order, i.e., first [1-9] and then [A-Z]."
msgstr ""

#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:139
msgid "In order to better handle legacy equipment designed to operate on ASCII payloads, the compressed CWT is encoded as ASCII using <a0>Base45</a0> before being encoded into a 2D barcode."
msgstr ""

#: input/pagecontent/hcert_spec.md:170
msgid "Instead, the primary validity mechanism is the presence of the certificate on the most recent version of that certificate list."
msgstr ""

